# Sample requests for the URL shortener (Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client).
# Run the API first: `dotnet run --project src` (http://localhost:5265) or `docker compose up` (http://localhost:8080).
# Make sure Shortener__BaseUrl matches the host you use so returned short URLs resolve.

@host = http://localhost:5265
@code = REPLACE_WITH_A_CODE_FROM_THE_CREATE_RESPONSE

### Create a short URL (201; 200 if the URL already has an active link)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/shorten
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://www.example.com/very/long/url",
  "expiryDays": 30
}

### Redirect (302; 404 unknown, 410 expired)
GET {{host}}/{{code}}

### Update the target and optionally reset the expiry
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/shorten/{{code}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.org/new-target",
  "expiryDays": 10
}

### Delete a link and its click history (204)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/shorten/{{code}}

### Analytics: totals, unique visitors, clicks per country
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/{{code}}

### Daily clicks (UTC days, inclusive; defaults to the last 30 days)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/{{code}}/daily?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31

### Clicks per country
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/{{code}}/countries

### Clicks per browser
GET {{host}}/api/v1/analytics/{{code}}/browsers

### Health (Healthy / Degraded when Redis is down / Unhealthy when SQL Server is down)
GET {{host}}/health
